{"data":{"id":"10.5281/zenodo.23604797","type":"dois","attributes":{"doi":"10.5281/zenodo.23604797","prefix":"10.5281","suffix":"zenodo.23604797","identifiers":[{"identifier":"oai:zenodo.org:23604797","identifierType":"oai"}],"alternateIdentifiers":[{"alternateIdentifierType":"oai","alternateIdentifier":"oai:zenodo.org:23604797"}],"creators":[{"name":"Carroll, Jeremy H.","nameType":"Personal","givenName":"Jeremy H.","familyName":"Carroll","nameIdentifiers":[],"affiliation":[]}],"titles":[{"title":"Observer - Relative Control of Cochain Residuals"},{"title":"A finite mathematical construction with explicit evidence boundaries","titleType":"Subtitle"}],"publisher":"Zenodo","container":{},"publicationYear":2026,"subjects":[{"subject":"observer object"},{"subject":"finite evaluation"},{"subject":"finite obstruction calculus"},{"subject":"obstruction theory"},{"subject":"observer-relative-measurement"},{"subject":"authority firewall"},{"subject":"finite descent"},{"subject":"proposer checker separation"},{"subject":"proof-carrying evaluation"},{"subject":"evaluation structure"},{"subject":"finite cochain complex"},{"subject":"gauge-dependent magnitude"},{"subject":"declared observer"},{"subject":"terminalizer"},{"subject":"quotient residual"},{"subject":"repair coboundary"}],"contributors":[],"dates":[{"date":"2026-10-23","dateType":"Issued"}],"language":"en","types":{"ris":"GEN","bibtex":"misc","citeproc":"article","schemaOrg":"CreativeWork","resourceType":"","resourceTypeGeneral":"Preprint"},"relatedIdentifiers":[{"relationType":"IsVersionOf","relatedIdentifier":"10.5281/zenodo.20652483","relatedIdentifierType":"DOI"}],"relatedItems":[],"sizes":[],"formats":[],"version":"v2.1.3 Pre-Print","rightsList":[{"rights":"Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International","rightsUri":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode","schemeUri":"https://spdx.org/licenses/","rightsIdentifier":"cc-by-4.0","rightsIdentifierScheme":"SPDX"},{"rights":"Copyright (C) 2026 Jeremy H. Carroll, Author","rightsUri":"http://rightsstatements.org/vocab/InC/1.0/"}],"descriptions":[{"description":"Abstract\n\nWe study finite candidate-selection policies constrained by several coordinate observers. Each observer specifies a projection, positive weights, a space of removable differences and a closure map. The policy bounds the observer-relative quotient residual, the closure residual and their ratio. We distinguish two coordinate estimates: a weighted norm bounds the coordinates of its input, whereas a quotient seminorm bounds coordinates only of a selected minimizing residual. Complete coordinate coverage does not remove this distinction. A one-edge example has zero quotient residual and arbitrarily large raw coordinates, even with complete observation. We give the corrected estimates, counterexamples to stronger transfer claims and a finite ranking rule. The supplied Lean development treats integer weighted norms; a numerical reference implementation additionally evaluates projected quotient problems.\n\nWhy This Matters\n\nThe paper distinguishes what its diagnostic inequalities measure from stronger claims that do not follow. Explicit definitions and counterexamples make the selection policy and its limits inspectable.\n\nCore Theorems\n\nThe numbered propositions and proofs in the manuscript state their domains and hypotheses. The revision separates quotient residuals, input norms, discrete formal lemmas and numerical evaluations rather than treating them as equivalent.\n\nFormal Verification and Computational Artifacts\n\nThe package includes source code, tests, a pinned standalone Lean project, an explicit declaration census and source-bound rendered files. The quick start gives commands for replay. Each formal result retains the scope described in the manuscript; test outcomes do not supply a theorem beyond that scope.\n\nScope Boundaries and Non-Claims\n\nCoordinate coverage does not bound raw cochains by a quotient residual. The corrected theorem bounds selected residuals, or raw vectors under an explicit weighted-input-norm assumption. The reference linear program uses floating-point arithmetic.\n\nReproduction\n\nSee [quick_start.md](quick_start.md) for installation, tests, the Lean census, rendering and independent archive checks. The manuscript and documentation use CC-BY-4.0; software and tests use Apache-2.0.\n\nRelated Identifiers and Citations\n\nVerified scholarly sources are listed in [references.md](references.md).The new revision has no assigned DOI. The previous record is [10.5281/zenodo.20214468](https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.20214468); its verified parent is [10.5281/zenodo.20214467](https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.20214467). The metadata records these version relationships.","descriptionType":"Abstract"}],"geoLocations":[],"fundingReferences":[],"xml":"","url":"https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.23604797","contentUrl":null,"metadataVersion":0,"schemaVersion":"http://datacite.org/schema/kernel-4","source":"api","isActive":true,"state":"findable","reason":null,"viewCount":0,"viewsOverTime":[],"downloadCount":0,"downloadsOverTime":[],"referenceCount":0,"citationCount":0,"citationsOverTime":[],"partCount":0,"partOfCount":0,"versionCount":0,"versionOfCount":1,"created":"2026-10-23T21:14:21.000Z","registered":"2026-10-23T21:14:22.000Z","published":"2026","updated":"2026-10-23T21:14:22.000Z"},"relationships":{"client":{"data":{"id":"cern.zenodo","type":"clients"}},"provider":{"data":{"id":"cern","type":"providers"}},"media":{"data":{"id":"10.5281/zenodo.23604797","type":"media"}},"references":{"data":[]},"citations":{"data":[]},"parts":{"data":[]},"partOf":{"data":[]},"versions":{"data":[]},"versionOf":{"data":[{"id":"10.5281/zenodo.20652483","type":"dois"}]}}}}